  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 5.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gif man deacon tihtlige, þe regollice libbe, anfealdre spæce, nime twegen his gehadan ⁊ ladige hine mid þam.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5.1" corresp="#wit-a">Gif man diacon tihlige, þe reollice libbe, anfealdre spræce, nime twegen his gehadan ⁊ ladige hine mid þam.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5.1" corresp="#wit-q">Diaconus regularis in simplici compellatione cum duobus,</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="5a.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gif man deacon tihtlige þe regollice libbe anfealdre spæce, nime twegen his gehadan ⁊ ladige hine mid þam.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">If a simple accusation is brought against a deacon who lives according to a rule, he shall take two supporters of the same ecclesiastical rank and clear himself with their help.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn ein Diakon, der kanonisch lebt, mit einfacher Anklage bezichtigt wird, so nehme er zwei seiner Standesgenossen und reinige sich mit denen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a deacon who lives according to a rule is charged with a simple accusation, let him take two of his fellow-clergy and clear himself with them.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VIII Atr 20.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
